@w0xlt I prefer the existing wording:

> callers pass the parent hash of an existing template

The function doesn't know where the caller got its hash.

I tried another approach: `submitSolution()` returns a `SubmittedBlock` capability instead of the block itself, so the client can fetch it later with `getBlock()`, only if and when it needs it. The template stays immutable and there's no mutex.

```
interface SubmittedBlock $Proxy.wrap("interfaces::SubmittedBlock") {
    destroy @0 (context :Proxy.Context) -> ();
    getBlock @1 (context: Proxy.Context) -> (result: Data);
}

submitSolution @10 (...) -> (reason: Text, debug: Text, accepted: Bool, result: SubmittedBlock);
```

Benchmarked it and got no performance regression with this approach.

Draft:

Bitcoin Core diff: https://github.com/ViniciusCestarii/bitcoin/commit/5c7fe8ee23cac873df8645b566150cc864e4c729
sv2-tp diff: https://github.com/ViniciusCestarii/sv2-tp/commit/7faa751ed160e1f210ad4644a1797bfdb62e1388

This gets the immutable template without the regression and without waiting for the libmultiprocess improvements. Happy to open it as a followup PR.
